# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# SECRETS
#
# server/.env holds the database URL and both JWT signing secrets. A
# repository is the most common place a credential leaks from, and a
# secret that has been committed is compromised even after it is
# deleted, because it stays in the history.
#
# .env.example is committed on purpose: it documents which variables
# exist without carrying a single real value.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# DEPENDENCIES AND BUILD OUTPUT
#
# Both are reproducible from package-lock.json and the source. Committing
# them makes every diff unreadable and the clone enormous.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
client/dist/
*.tsbuildinfo

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# LOCAL NOISE
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
npm-debug.log*
*.log
coverage/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea/

# Uploaded or generated artefacts that belong to a running instance,
# not to the source.
uploads/
*.pdf
!server/docs/**/*.pdf
